This project's full instructions live in AGENTS.md at the repo root. Read it first, before any code work.

Cross-harness governance lives in agent-rules/. ADR rationale lives in docs/adr/.

High-priority rules (full text in agent-rules/):

1. Use the latest stable version when adding any dependency. Run `npm view <pkg> version` and `npm view <pkg> dist-tags` before installing. Pin caret (^) for app deps, exact for tools that affect output (Biome, TypeScript). Never trust your training-data memory of versions.

2. Before adding a new dependency: (a) run `pnpm ls --depth=0` to confirm an existing package doesn't already cover the concern, (b) check agent-rules/architecture.md and the project spec for an existing decision, (c) propose to the user with name, why, alternatives, version, and weekly-download signal, (d) wait for explicit confirmation before installing.

3. Locate the canonical spec at session start (SPEC.md, PRD.md, docs/spec/*). Read it before code. Re-anchor before architectural moves. If the spec is wrong, propose an edit; don't drift around it.

4. The OpenAPI contract (openapi.json, generated from Zod schemas) is the load-bearing API contract. Server function input shape must match it; CI enforces this via scripts/check-openapi-contract.mjs.

5. For TanStack-area work, run `npx @tanstack/intent load <package>#<skill>` before writing code. Skills are version-locked to installed packages and override training data.

6. For external library guidance (Cloudflare, Microsoft Foundry, Entra, Better Auth, etc.), prefer the configured MCP servers (Cloudflare Docs, Microsoft Learn, Context7) over training data. Configuration is in .claude/settings.json; Codex equivalents in agent-rules/codex-config.md.

7. Documentation lookup order: agent-rules → TanStack Intent skills → configured MCP servers → llms.txt at vendor domain → vendor official docs → web search → training data (last resort, must verify).

8. All identity reads go through getCurrentUser(request) in src/lib/auth/. Don't import Better Auth directly from route guards or server functions.

9. Don't write "what" comments. Don't use em dashes. Use kebab-case for filenames. Always write "Microsoft 365" and "Microsoft Foundry" in full.

10. Don't override locked decisions silently. Locked decisions have ADRs in docs/adr/. If you're tempted to deviate, read the ADR, then propose a spec edit.
